# Required live Supabase configuration. Copy to .env.local for local development.
# In Vercel, set both variables for the deployment environments you will use.
# Values are built into the browser bundle: only use the public anon/publishable key.
# Never put a service-role/secret key here. Do not commit filled-in environment files.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional: web push notifications. Without it the app deploys exactly as before and the
# settings switch stays off; every other tab is unaffected.
#
# Generate a keypair once, on any machine:
#   npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
#
# Then:
#   * put the PUBLIC half here (it is public: the browser hands it to its own push
#     service to prove a notification really came from Nooki). Set it for Production and
#     any Preview you test, and redeploy — Vite inlines it at build time.
#   * set the PRIVATE half as the VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY secret on the `send-push` Edge
#     Function (supabase secrets set VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=...). It must never appear here,
#     in any VITE_ variable, or in the repository.
#
# Then deploy the function and add the Database Webhook on `messages` — the step-by-step
# list is under "Push notifications" in README.md.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
